```javascript
vi.mock("@/features/auth", () => ({
  useSession: () => ({ session: { status: "authenticated", data: null }, logout: vi.fn() }),
  SessionProvider: ({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) => children,
}));
```

But `useOrgWorkspaceSelection` tries to access `session.data.memberships` when `session.status === "authenticated"`, which fails because `data` is `null`.


I need to add a null check in `useOrgWorkspaceSelection` to guard against accessing properties on null data before trying to read the memberships array.

